  "notes": "R79b addresses identifier consistency across reporting, audit, and export contexts. Primary evidence reveals three core concerns: (1) financial outputs do not align cleanly across billing contexts; (2) privacy-preserving identifiers in audit views hinder non-technical auditor review; (3) exported artifacts do not match underlying platform interpretation. The requirement depends on resolving conflicts between formal specification identifiers, business-facing aliases, and warehouse-facing operational identifiers. Multiple implementation tickets (JIRA-REP-701, JIRA-ITEM-301, JIRA-REP-703) confirm that identifier format and source-of-truth decisions remain unresolved. Context evidence (E12–E17) indicates related gaps in identifier alias consistency and historical data handling. The operative context captures the intended consistency rules; exceptions document privacy-preserving allowances; conflicts_or_obsolete lists current mismatches; gaps_or_uncertainties identifies unresolved design decisions that must be clarified before test generation can proceed.\" Filtered abstract or low-relevance operative statements: Identifier consistency must be maintained across reporting outputs, exported files, and billing records | Reporting must use a consistent identifier model aligned with the formal specification | Authorized users must have access to controlled identity-resolution paths for audit review",
